<article class="page">
  <header>
    <h1>How this site is built</h1>
    <p class="lede">This site has a carbon budget, and the budget is enforced: a page that goes
       over it fails the build and is never published.</p>
  </header>

  <section aria-labelledby="measured">
    <h2 id="measured">What it weighs</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table, scrolls sideways on small screens">
      <table class="data">
        <caption class="visually-hidden">Measured weight of the home page against the budget</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Home page</th><th scope="col">Measured</th><th scope="col">Budget</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Total weight on first visit</td><td class="num">79 KB</td><td class="num">150 KB</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Emissions per visit</td><td class="num">0.010 g CO<sub>2</sub>e</td><td class="num">0.03 g</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Stylesheet, compressed</td><td class="num">3.0 KB</td><td class="num">8 KB</td></tr>
          <tr><td>JavaScript</td><td class="num">&lt; 1 KB</td><td class="num">1 KB</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Requests to other companies while loading</td><td class="num">0</td><td class="num">0</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Measured on 5 November 2026. The median desktop home page weighed 2,862 KB in the
       <a href="https://almanac.httparchive.org/en/2025/page-weight">2025 Web Almanac</a>:
       this one is about thirty-six times lighter. Every page carries its own figure in the
       footer, computed when the site is built.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="method">
    <h2 id="method">How it is measured</h2>
    <p>With the <a href="https://sustainablewebdesign.org/estimating-digital-emissions/">Sustainable
       Web Design Model</a>, version 4: 0.3 kWh for every gigabyte transferred, at the global
       average grid intensity of 494 g CO<sub>2</sub>e per kWh. Because the hosting runs on
       verified renewable energy, the share of the data centre is removed from the count.
       The model is an estimate, not a meter. Its most useful lesson is that more than half
       of the energy is spent on the reader's device, which is why this site asks that device
       to do as little as possible.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="choices">
    <h2 id="choices">The choices, and why</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Fonts already on your device.</strong> No font is downloaded, so nothing is
          fetched from another company and nothing shifts while the page loads.</li>
      <li><strong>HTML and CSS, almost no JavaScript.</strong> One small script turns a talk
          link into a player when you click it. With JavaScript switched off, the link still
          works.</li>
      <li><strong>Images in AVIF</strong>, with WebP for older browsers, sized for the space
          they occupy, with location and camera metadata removed.</li>
      <li><strong>Videos load only when asked for.</strong> An embedded player costs more than
          half a megabyte to every visitor, including those who never press play.</li>
      <li><strong>No analytics, no cookies, no forms.</strong> See the
          <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Static pages</strong>, generated with <a href="https://www.11ty.dev/">Eleventy</a>.
          Nothing is computed when you visit.</li>
      <li><strong>Green hosting</strong>: GitHub Pages, delivered through Fastly, verified by
          <a href="https://www.thegreenwebfoundation.org/green-web-check/">The Green Web Foundation</a>.
          The details are in <a href="/carbon.txt">carbon.txt</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="not-done">
    <h2 id="not-done">What was not done</h2>
    <p>A dark theme follows your system setting, but it is there for reading comfort. It saves
       energy only on some screens, and too little to claim. The site does not adapt to how
       clean the electricity grid is at the moment you visit: a promising idea, not yet worth
       its complexity here.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="access">
    <h2 id="access">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>The target is WCAG 2.2 at level AA: text contrast above the AAA threshold in both themes,
       full keyboard navigation, targets at least 44 pixels high, motion reduced when your
       system asks for it. Automated checks with axe-core found no violations on 5 November
       2026. Automated checks do not catch everything: if something does not work for you,
       please <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">tell me</a>.</p>
  </section>

